  description="MC3R is the melanocortin receptor that reports nutritional state. Mice without it do not mobilise fat in a fast, do not anticipate a scheduled meal, and do not time puberty to whether they are fed. They get mildly fat without eating more. MC4R is the appetite switch; this is the receptor that decides what to do with the news that food has stopped."
  seoDescription="MC3R reports nutritional state: the fasting response, meal anticipation, and the timing of puberty. Losing it fattens mice without making them eat more."
